Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 15:10:33 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Remove unauthenticated duplicate seed-production endpoint
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

POST /api/setup/seed-production had no auth guard in front of it at
all — it relied only on an optional SEED_SECRET_KEY body param that
silently no-ops the check entirely if that env var was never set. It
duplicated the now-fixed scripts/seed-trips.ts via a separate,
unrelated seedSampleTrips() in server/services/seedService.ts: only 3
trips, capitalized region values ("Central") that don't match
trip-card.tsx's lowercase region-color lookup, and it created a
'CeylonX Admin' user under a hardcoded pre-rebrand email/id.

The one seeding path admins should use is the already admin-gated
POST /api/admin/seed-data (server/routes/adminRoutes.ts), which calls
the real, fixed scripts/seed-trips.ts. Deleted seedService.ts and the
route entirely rather than patching either, since nothing else
referenced it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
